      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "<!-- pr-pundit-live:primus-1385-4c95e1ed -->\n### PR Pundit review\n1 finding.\n\n| # | | Finding | Where |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 🔵 | Next documented lock regeneration will churn two `# via` comments: this PR changed their paths | `docs/sphinx/requirements.txt:193` |\n\n<details><summary>Nits and less certain findings (1)</summary>\n\n**1. Next documented lock regeneration will churn two `# via` comments: this PR changed their paths** (`docs/sphinx/requirements.txt:193`)\n\nTwo provenance comments changed from `# via -r docs/sphinx/requirements.in` to `# via -r requirements.in` (for `rocm-docs-core` and `sphinxcontrib-mermaid`). The header still documents `pip-compile docs/sphinx/requirements.in` run from the repo root, so the lock is internally inconsistent and the next regeneration from the root will flip these lines back as unrelated churn. Keep the original paths, or update the header command to match.\n\n**Who is affected:** Maintainers who next regenerate docs/sphinx/requirements.txt with the documented root-level `pip-compile` command; no runtime or install impact.\n\n_Checked against the code by an independent pass._\n\n</details>",
